 "registry_overlay": {
  "$comment": "Plan B draft (P3, 11-01): what the visual group's node registry adds for an external node, as data. It extends P1's node-registry.json (bound selects and stop lines, kept as they are) with: binding, frame (the core's frame and plot box), items (how the core expands a node's items from its binds, by a closed set of field kinds), marks (one mark per item or per item part, a closed shape, and for every field of that shape EITHER a declared field -> channel -> scale the core recomputes, OR the field is free and held only by constraints: inside the frame and tied to its text), texts (which item fields are printed, each tied to its mark by a closed relation) and the text size. Geometry comes in two kinds (owner 11-01): value-determined fields (length, angle, point, colour) the core recomputes from the declared scale and the node's must be equal within tol_px; placement the values cannot decide (labels, avoidance) is held to three constraints only: inside the frame, no two text boxes overlap, each text next to its own mark (max_px). The scale kind, domain source and range are the core's: the range is the plot box the core sends; no scale parameter is ever taken from a node. An entry naming a check kind, channel, scale, relation, field kind, shape or frame the core does not compute, or leaving a shape field neither declared nor free, is refused when the registry loads.",
  "extends": "../../p1-page-tree-1101/node-registry.json",
